ress the margin on Election Day.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike DeWine (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Ohio's open governor's race pits Democrat Amy Acton against Republican Vivek Ramaswamy after two terms of Mike DeWine, who is term-limited. The state leans Republican on paper, but recent polls consistently show Acton ahead by roughly four to five points, including surveys from pollsters with no partisan tilt and one with Republican sponsorship. Most expert raters call the race Lean D, with only one rating it a Tossup and one Likely D.\n\nRamaswamy has vastly outspent Acton and holds a large cash advantage, yet the polling gap has held steady into the final days. Prediction markets price Acton's chances near 80 percent. The race remains competitive enough that a strong Republican turnout operation or late voter movement could narrow the result, but the weight of the evidence favors Acton heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.545, "margin": 0.49}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5929, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5919, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6166, "margin": 1.3}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5684, "margin": 1.2}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.592, "margin": 1.4}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6233, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.662, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6672, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6954, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6724, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6809, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7082, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7607, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7343, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-